e Hive initial load. Dynamically import the Cockpit modules on the first Cockpit navigation, render the cockpit shell/data first, and load the robot/3D modules after (or on idle). Keep the Hive rendering exactly as now. Keep exports/tests working; the boot must remain testable with injected deps.\n- Raise the visible poll interval to 5000 ms and stop polling when document.hidden; resume immediately on visibilitychange. Keep the existing poll callback behavior.\n\nPart 3 - tests: add focused tests for: 304 on ETag, gzip when accepted and not when not, cache headers per asset type, snapshot cache key/ETag, lazy Cockpit/robot imports (Hive initial import graph excludes them), poll interval/pause. Keep every existing command-center and watch-assets test green (the full suite runs before merge). Verify: node --import ./tests/_isolate-config.mjs --test tests/command-center-boot.test.mjs tests/command-center-routes-flag.test.mjs tests/command-center-flag.test.mjs tests/watch-assets.test.mjs tests/watch-assets-browser-safe.test.mjs tests/command-center-perf-budget.test.mjs -> all pass (create the perf budget test with static budgets if the job can; otherwise a focused server test). Report the payload/caching changes and counts.",
